  "question": {
    "text": "If a curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and satisfies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then for what value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>62</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>?</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [
